  "P1 Standard Sega mapper semantics (R4 of DECOMP-1D). Slot 0 is bank 0: the only stores to the slot-0 mapper register $FFFD are in the boot sequence (listed in the census). Slot 2 is bank $1D for the nested dispatcher (R1's assumption for the routine at $8000); a record pointer into slot 1 or 2 is never interpreted (its bank is unverified).",
  "P2 Player and level inputs (collisions, ring pickups, pressed buttons) are adversarial: every transition the ROM permits is treated as possible. A path is *grounded* when every step is permitted by the code alone and none rests on a dependency this task did not discharge.",
  "P3 Register-addressed writers whose pointer is computed (not an immediate) and block moves with an unresolved destination are listed, never assumed benign; this is DECOMP-1D assumption R2 and it stays open.",
  "P4 The discovered-code universe is the DECOMP-1D walk; byte-pattern hits outside it (object-callback code in banked ROM) are reported separately and are classified by the same value-source analysis where the encoding is unambiguous."
 ],
