   "id": "U1",
   "title": "zone-complete trigger inside a special stage",
   "text": "D293 bit 4 is raised by $303ED (guarded only by act >= 2) and by the $50 stores at $7BB2A/$7BB6E, all in object-callback code outside the discovered universe. The special-stage dispatcher ($176F) honours bit 4, so a zone-complete while the zone is 8..12 would run the zone increment on a special-stage zone. Not excluded; modelled as an ungrounded edge."
  },
  {
   "id": "U2",
   "title": "emerald masks are object-supplied",
   "text": "$D2CC is written at $794A7 (OR with the object byte IX+$3F) and $7BB69 (OR $20). The masks are not derived here, so a special-stage zone above 8 (which needs emerald bits 0..3 set) is not grounded."
  },
  {
   "id": "U3",
   "title": "special stages loaded from a garbage record pointer",
   "text": "For a special-stage zone (8..12) the loader's act-table walk leaves the nine records at act 9 (zones 8, 9, 11) or act 6 (zones 10, 12); the record pointer is then record data, read through an unverified bank. Whether such a stage can be left is not known."
  },
  {
   "id": "U4",
   "title": "allocator / kernel-vector route to a type-5 slot",
   "text": "Inherited from DECOMP-1D-R1 (ALLOCATOR lemma): only the direct callers of $1CD3 are enumerated; the kernel vector $0374 can be entered through callback stubs with an unknown C."
  },
  {
   "id": "U5",
   "title": "register-addressed block moves",
   "text": "Block moves whose destination is not an immediate (listed in the census) could, in principle, cover the zone/act bytes."
  },
  {
   "id": "U6",
   "title": "D2C8 and reaching 100 rings are player-supplied",
   "text": "Treated as adversarial inputs (premise P2); the code permits both."
  }
 ],
